Test the kernel RT throttle feature, that limits the RT rq's cpu runtime, the
default is 0.95s in 1s. If RT_RUNTIME_SHARE is disabled (default), no-RT tasks
such as SCHED_NORMAL would get chance to run, this rescue the starvation caused
by priority preempt and some priority inversion situation such as RT tasks need
resource from normal task, but normal task don't have chance to run.

